[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Intertube.Stub core library requirements
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: intertube.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document states the requirements for the core of Intertube.Stub: the types in ``src/Intertube.Stub/*.cs`` and ``src/Intertube.Stub/Internal/`` that make up the stream servers (``TcpServer``, ``UnixServer``), the ``Connection`` they hand to handlers, TLS, the ready-made handlers and protocol helpers (``Handler``, ``LineResponder``, ``LineMatcher``, ``Conversation``), fault injection (``FaultOptions``), transcripts with their assertion and wait helpers, and ``UdpServer``. The ready-made SMTP and SFTP servers are covered by their own documents.

The key words "shall", "should" and "may" carry the meaning given in RFC 2119. Requirements with status Active describe current, intended behaviour; Deferred and Rejected entries record review decisions and their reasons.

VERIFIED_BY lists the automated tests that demonstrate a requirement, one per line as ``TypeName.MemberName``: the C# test class and method, or for F# the module name and the test's double-backticked name. Tests live in ``tests/Intertube.Stub.Tests``, ``examples/Intertube.Stub.Examples``, ``examples/Intertube.Stub.FSharp`` and ``samples/RedisLite.Tests``. A line starting with "Review:" names a file or document that shows the behaviour where no automated test covers it; such requirements also carry the comment "No automated test."
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: General properties

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-GEN-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Target frameworks
STATEMENT: >>>
The ``Intertube.Stub`` package shall target ``net8.0`` and ``net10.0``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj (TargetFrameworks); .github/workflows/ci.yml builds and tests both frameworks
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-GEN-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Minimal dependencies
STATEMENT: >>>
The core library shall have no package dependencies other than ``System.IO.Pipelines``, and that one only for ``net8.0`` (it is part of the shared framework on ``net10.0``).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A test double should not drag third-party packages into the test projects that use it.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj (PackageReference items)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-GEN-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Native AOT compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The library shall be marked ``IsAotCompatible`` and shall build without trimming or AOT analyzer warnings, so it can be used from Native AOT and trimmed test hosts.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Intertube.Stub.csproj (IsAotCompatible); .github/workflows/ci.yml builds with -warnaserror
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-GEN-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Loopback binding by default
STATEMENT: >>>
``TcpServer.Listen(int, ...)`` and ``UdpServer.Listen(int, ...)`` shall bind to ``127.0.0.1``; binding to any other address shall require the caller to pass an ``IPEndPoint`` explicitly. Port 0 shall select a free ephemeral port, reported by ``Port``.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A stub accepts whatever it is sent; it must not be reachable from the network unless a test asks for that.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- UdpServerTests.Replies_ToEachDatagram
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-GEN-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Thread safety
STATEMENT: >>>
Server properties (``Errors``, ``ActiveConnections``, ``Transcript``) and transcript queries, assertions and waits shall be safe to call from any thread while handlers are running; collection-valued properties shall return snapshots. A ``Connection``, like a ``Stream``, shall support one concurrent reader and one concurrent writer.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Concurrent_HandlesClientsInParallel
- RobustnessTests.MaxConcurrency_LimitsHandlersRunningAtOnce
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-GEN-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Throwing log callback is contained
STATEMENT: >>>
An exception thrown by the ``ServerOptions.Log`` or ``UdpServerOptions.Log`` callback shall be swallowed: it shall not fail the handler, be added to ``Errors``, stop the server or make ``DisposeAsync`` throw.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
xUnit's ``ITestOutputHelper.WriteLine`` throws once its test has finished, while a server may still be logging its shutdown.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.ALogCallbackThatThrows_DoesNotStopTheServer
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The UDP path uses the same guard (``ConnectionTranscript.SafeLog``) but has no test of its own.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Stream server lifecycle

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Listen starts the server
STATEMENT: >>>
``TcpServer.Listen`` shall bind, start listening and start accepting connections before it returns, running the given handler (a ``Func<Connection, Task>`` or an ``IConnectionHandler``) once per accepted connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Listen on a chosen endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
``TcpServer.Listen(IPEndPoint, ...)`` shall bind to the given address and port, including IPv6 and wildcard addresses, and expose the bound address as ``EndPoint``. If binding fails the listening socket shall be disposed and the exception rethrown; a null endpoint or handler shall throw ``ArgumentNullException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.WildcardBind_ClientsConnectThroughLoopback
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
IPv6 binding and the bind-failure path have no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Host maps wildcard binds to loopback
STATEMENT: >>>
``TcpServer.Host`` shall return the bound address as a string, except that ``IPAddress.Any`` shall map to ``127.0.0.1`` and ``IPAddress.IPv6Any`` to ``::1``, so the value can always be used by a client to connect.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.WildcardBind_ClientsConnectThroughLoopback
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connections are numbered and recorded on accept
STATEMENT: >>>
Each accepted connection shall be given an ``Id`` starting at 1 and increasing per server, and shall be added to ``Transcript`` with a "connected from" event before its handler runs, including connections that wait behind ``MaxConcurrency``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Transcript_ToString_IsReadable
- RetryExample.RecoversFromTwoResets
- TcpServerTests.Sequential_HandlesOneConnectionAtATime
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Concurrent handlers by default
STATEMENT: >>>
With ``MaxConcurrency`` null (the default) every accepted connection shall run its handler at once, in parallel with the others. ``ActiveConnections`` shall report the number of handlers still running.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Concurrent_HandlesClientsInParallel
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MaxConcurrency limits running handlers
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``ServerOptions.MaxConcurrency`` is set to n, at most n handlers shall run at once; further connections shall be accepted and recorded, then wait for a free slot. ``ServerOptions.Sequential`` shall be equivalent to ``MaxConcurrency = 1``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.MaxConcurrency_LimitsHandlersRunningAtOnce
- TcpServerTests.Sequential_HandlesOneConnectionAtATime
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MaxConcurrency validation
STATEMENT: >>>
Creating a stream server with ``MaxConcurrency`` less than 1 shall throw ``ArgumentOutOfRangeException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/StreamServer.cs (StreamServer constructor)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connection closed when the handler returns
STATEMENT: >>>
When a handler completes, by returning or by throwing, the server shall close its connection gracefully (as ``Connection.CloseAsync``) unless it is already closed or reset.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- ConfigClientTests.scripted conversation: SET then GET, exactly in that order
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ConnectAsync opens a client connection
STATEMENT: >>>
``StreamServer.ConnectAsync`` shall open a client-side ``Connection`` to the server (through loopback for a wildcard bind) with the same read and write helpers, the server's encoding, newline and ``ReadTimeout``, no faults, and its own transcript that is not part of ``Server.Transcript``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadLinesAsync_StreamsUntilClientCloses
- RobustnessTests.WildcardBind_ClientsConnectThroughLoopback
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_CloseMode_SendsEndOfStream
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler failures are captured
STATEMENT: >>>
An exception escaping a handler shall be added to ``Errors`` and recorded as a "handler failed: Type: message" event on the connection's transcript; it shall not stop the server or affect other connections.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.HandlerErrors_AreCapturedNotLost
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_MismatchIsReportedWithStep
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Expected endings are not errors
STATEMENT: >>>
The following shall not be added to ``Errors``: a reset or disconnect by the peer, a ``ConnectionTerminatedException`` from a fault, any exception after this side has closed or reset the connection, any exception once the server is stopping, and a ``TlsHandshakeException``.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
These are what a fault-injection test sets out to cause; reporting them as failures would make ``ThrowIfFaulted`` useless.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ClientReset_IsRecordedButNotAnError
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_ResetsMidMessage
- FaultTests.FaultsCanChangePerConnection
- RobustnessTests.FailedTlsHandshake_IsAnEvent_NotAHandlerError
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ThrowIfFaulted
STATEMENT: >>>
``ThrowIfFaulted`` shall throw an ``AggregateException`` containing every recorded handler error if there is at least one, and do nothing otherwise.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.HandlerErrors_AreCapturedNotLost
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: WaitForErrorsAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``WaitForErrorsAsync(count, timeout)`` shall complete once at least ``count`` (default 1) handler errors have been recorded, and shall throw ``TimeoutException`` including the transcript if that does not happen within ``timeout`` (default 5 seconds).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.HandlerErrors_AreCapturedNotLost
- TcpServerTests.ReadTimeout_FailsTheHandler
- RobustnessTests.Conversation_OnMismatchAppliesToComputedReplies
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Graceful stop
STATEMENT: >>>
``StopAsync`` and ``DisposeAsync`` shall stop accepting, cancel ``Stopping`` and every connection's ``CancellationToken``, and wait up to ``ServerOptions.ShutdownTimeout`` (default 2 seconds) for running handlers to finish. A handler that honours cancellation shall let the stop complete promptly, and its client shall see the connection end.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Dispose_StopsPromptlyEvenWithBlockedHandlers
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Forced reset after ShutdownTimeout
STATEMENT: >>>
Connections whose handlers are still running after ``ShutdownTimeout`` shall be reset (recorded as "reset"); a handler that still does not finish shall be abandoned after a second ``ShutdownTimeout`` so that stopping always completes.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.Stop_ResetsAHandlerThatIgnoresCancellation_AfterShutdownTimeout
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stop is idempotent and does not throw for handler errors
STATEMENT: >>>
Calling ``StopAsync`` or ``DisposeAsync`` more than once shall return the same stop operation. Stopping shall not throw because a handler failed; handler failures are reported only through ``Errors``, ``ThrowIfFaulted`` and ``WaitForErrorsAsync``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.HandlerErrors_AreCapturedNotLost
- RobustnessTests.ALogCallbackThatThrows_DoesNotStopTheServer
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Calling stop twice has no automated test (see ``StreamServer.StopAsync``, which returns a cached ``Lazy<Task>``).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Accept loop survives client failures
STATEMENT: >>>
A client that resets before or while it is being accepted, or a transient accept error, shall not stop the accept loop; the server shall back off briefly and keep accepting.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/StreamServer.cs (AcceptLoopAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SRV-018
STATUS: Rejected
TITLE: Dispose throws when a handler failed
STATEMENT: >>>
``DisposeAsync`` would throw an ``AggregateException`` if any handler had failed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Throwing from ``await using`` at the end of a test hides the test's real failure (an assertion that already failed would be replaced by the disposal exception) and makes cleanup paths throw. ``ThrowIfFaulted`` and ``WaitForErrorsAsync`` are the explicit opt-in for surfacing handler failures.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ITS-SRV-016

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Unix domain sockets

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UNIX-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Temporary socket path
STATEMENT: >>>
``UnixServer.Listen(null, ...)`` shall bind a Unix domain socket at a fresh, unique path in the system temporary directory and expose it as ``Path``; the socket file shall exist while the server runs.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.UnixSocket_UsesTemporaryPathAndCleansUp
- DockerUnixSocketExample.ListsOnlyRunningContainers
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UNIX-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Temporary socket file is deleted on stop
STATEMENT: >>>
When a ``UnixServer`` created with a null path stops, it shall delete its socket file, ignoring I/O and permission errors.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.UnixSocket_UsesTemporaryPathAndCleansUp
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UNIX-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Caller-supplied path is left alone
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``UnixServer.Listen`` is given a path, the server shall bind to that path and shall not delete the socket file when it stops.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/StreamServer.cs (UnixServer.OnStopped)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UNIX-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Same features as TCP
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``UnixServer`` shall offer the same handler model, ``Connection`` API, transcript, errors, ``ConnectAsync`` and stop behaviour as ``TcpServer``, on Linux, macOS and Windows 10 or later.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.UnixSocket_UsesTemporaryPathAndCleansUp
- ClientTests.UnixSocket_Works
- DockerUnixSocketExample.Restart_PostsToTheRightEndpoint
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UNIX-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Abort on a Unix socket
STATEMENT: >>>
``Connection.Abort`` on a Unix domain socket, which has no TCP reset, shall close the socket immediately without a graceful shutdown and still record a "reset" event.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Connection.cs (Abort)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Connection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ReadLineAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReadLineAsync`` shall return the next line terminated by LF or CRLF, without the terminator, decoded with ``ServerOptions.Encoding`` (UTF-8 without BOM by default). At end of stream it shall return any unterminated remainder as a final line, then null.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadLinesAsync_StreamsUntilClientCloses
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The unterminated-final-line case has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ReadLinesAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReadLinesAsync`` shall yield each line as ``ReadLineAsync`` would until the peer closes the connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadLinesAsync_StreamsUntilClientCloses
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ReadUntilAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReadUntilAsync`` (byte or string delimiter) shall return the data before the delimiter and consume the delimiter. If the stream ends first it shall return null and leave any unterminated data buffered. An empty delimiter shall throw ``ArgumentException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.MixedFraming_LinesDelimitersAndExactBytesShareOneBuffer
- Hl7MllpExample.Messages_AreAcknowledged_OnOneConnection
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ReadExactlyAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReadExactlyAsync(count)`` shall return exactly ``count`` bytes, or throw ``EndOfStreamException`` if the stream ends first. A count of 0 shall return an empty array and a negative count shall throw ``ArgumentOutOfRangeException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.MixedFraming_LinesDelimitersAndExactBytesShareOneBuffer
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
- BinaryProtocolExample.RoundTrip
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ReadAsync and ReadToEndAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReadAsync(Memory<byte>)`` shall return as many buffered or newly arrived bytes as fit (at least one), or 0 at end of stream. ``ReadToEndAsync`` shall return everything received until the peer closes its side.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ClientReset_IsRecordedButNotAnError
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_CloseMode_SendsEndOfStream
- FaultTests.Corrupt_IsDeterministicForASeed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One shared input buffer
STATEMENT: >>>
All read helpers, ``Input`` (a ``PipeReader``) and ``Stream`` shall share one input buffer, so they can be mixed freely and no read helper loses data that another has buffered.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.MixedFraming_LinesDelimitersAndExactBytesShareOneBuffer
- TcpServerTests.PipeReaderInput_SupportsBinaryParsing
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stream view
STATEMENT: >>>
``Connection.Stream`` shall be a readable, writable, non-seekable ``Stream`` that reads from the shared buffer and writes through ``WriteAsync`` (so faults and the transcript apply); disposing it shall not close the connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Stream_CanBeUsedWithStandardReaders
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: MaxLineLength
STATEMENT: >>>
A line or delimited frame longer than ``ServerOptions.MaxLineLength`` (default 1 MiB) shall make ``ReadLineAsync`` or ``ReadUntilAsync`` throw ``InvalidDataException`` instead of buffering without bound.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.OverlongLine_GetsA500AndTheConnectionCloses_WithoutAHandlerError
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ReadTimeout
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``ServerOptions.ReadTimeout`` is set, a read that receives no data within that time shall record a "read timed out" event and throw ``TimeoutException``, which counts as a handler error. With no ``ReadTimeout`` (the default) reads shall wait indefinitely.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadTimeout_FailsTheHandler
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reads and writes observe cancellation
STATEMENT: >>>
Every read and write shall observe both the caller's ``CancellationToken`` and the connection's ``CancellationToken``, which is cancelled when the owning server starts to stop.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Dispose_StopsPromptlyEvenWithBlockedHandlers
- TcpServerTests.Concurrent_HandlesClientsInParallel
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Byte and text writes
STATEMENT: >>>
``WriteAsync(ReadOnlyMemory<byte>)`` shall send the bytes through the connection's faults and record them as sent. ``WriteAsync(string)`` shall send the text encoded with ``ServerOptions.Encoding`` exactly as given, with no terminator.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_CloseMode_SendsEndOfStream
- BinaryProtocolExample.RoundTrip
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Line writes
STATEMENT: >>>
``WriteLineAsync`` shall send the text followed by ``ServerOptions.NewLine`` (CRLF by default), and ``WriteLinesAsync`` shall send several lines, each followed by ``NewLine``, in a single write.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_ResetsMidMessage
- InstrumentExample.IdentifiesAndMeasures
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Output pipe
STATEMENT: >>>
``Connection.Output`` shall be a ``PipeWriter`` whose data is sent, through the connection's faults and transcript, when flushed. Pending output shall be flushed before a TLS upgrade and on a graceful close.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.DisconnectAfterViaOutput_StillRecordsTheClose
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Graceful close
STATEMENT: >>>
``CloseAsync`` (and ``DisposeAsync``) shall flush ``Output``, end TLS if active, send FIN, record a "closed" event, then drain input for up to one second so that unread client data does not turn the close into a reset that discards the last response. Each step shall be best effort, and calling it again shall have no further effect.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_CloseMode_SendsEndOfStream
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Abort
STATEMENT: >>>
``Abort`` shall drop the connection immediately with a TCP reset, including a connection part way through a graceful close, and record a "reset" event. It shall also cut a client that is idle while the handler has a read pending.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Abort_WhileTheHandlerIsReading_CutsAnIdleClient
- FaultTests.Reset_RefusesService
- ConfigClientTests.a reset on the first connection is retried
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: IsTerminated and Terminated
STATEMENT: >>>
``IsTerminated`` shall become true, and the ``Terminated`` token shall be cancelled, once this side closes or resets the connection (by the handler, a fault, an interceptor or server shutdown). The peer closing shall not set them. An exception thrown by a ``Terminated`` callback shall not prevent termination.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MessageTranscriptTests.Terminated_FiresOnAbort_ButNotWhenThePeerCloses
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Peer close
STATEMENT: >>>
When the peer closes its side, reads shall report end of stream (null or 0) and the transcript shall record "closed by peer" and become closed.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MessageTranscriptTests.Terminated_FiresOnAbort_ButNotWhenThePeerCloses
- TcpServerTests.ReadLinesAsync_StreamsUntilClientCloses
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Peer reset
STATEMENT: >>>
A reset by the peer during a read, write or hang shall be recorded as a "reset by peer" event, mark the transcript closed, and not count as a handler error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.PeerResetDuringAWrite_IsRecordedAsAReset
- TcpServerTests.ClientReset_IsRecordedButNotAnError
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: HangAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``HangAsync`` shall record a "hanging" event, then read and discard input without ever replying until the peer disconnects or the server stops. ``ReadTimeout`` shall not apply to it.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Hang_LetsClientTimeOut
- RobustnessTests.Hang_IgnoresReadTimeout
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Buffered-input check for protocol layers
STATEMENT: >>>
The library-internal ``HasBufferedInput`` shall report whether, and how many, received bytes are buffered but unread, without consuming them, so protocol layers can detect commands pipelined after STARTTLS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpProtocolTests.StartTls_WithPipelinedCommands_IsRefusedAndClosed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONN-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connection identity
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``Connection`` shall expose its ``Id`` (as in its transcript), ``RemoteEndPoint``, ``LocalEndPoint`` and underlying ``Socket``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RetryExample.RecoversFromTwoResets
- ConfigClientTests.a reset on the first connection is retried
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: TLS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Self-signed certificates on the fly
STATEMENT: >>>
``TlsOptions.SelfSigned(hostName)`` shall create options holding a fresh ECDSA P-256 server certificate with subject ``CN=hostName`` (default "localhost"), subject alternative names for ``hostName``, ``127.0.0.1`` and ``::1``, the server-authentication EKU, and validity from five minutes ago to seven days ahead, usable by the platform TLS stack on Windows, Linux and macOS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.ImplicitTls_WithSelfSignedCertificate
- ClientTests.Tls_WithAnOnTheFlyCertificate
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Each certificate is distinct
STATEMENT: >>>
Every call to ``TlsOptions.CreateSelfSignedCertificate`` or ``SelfSigned`` shall generate a new key pair, so two stubs never share a certificate.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TlsPinningExample.RejectsAnyOtherCertificate
- FtpExample.ImpostorCertificate_IsRejected
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: TrustServerCertificate
STATEMENT: >>>
``TlsOptions.TrustServerCertificate`` shall be a client validation callback that accepts exactly the options' ``Certificate`` (by certificate hash) and rejects any other or missing certificate.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.ImplicitTls_WithSelfSignedCertificate
- ImapExample.UnseenMessages_AreHandled_ThenFlaggedSeen
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Client certificates
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``ClientCertificateRequired`` is set the server shall request a client certificate; client certificates shall be validated by ``ClientCertificateValidation`` when given and otherwise accepted.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/TlsOptions.cs (ToServerOptions)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Protocol versions and ALPN
STATEMENT: >>>
``EnabledProtocols`` (default ``SslProtocols.None``, letting the OS choose) and ``ApplicationProtocols`` (ALPN) shall be applied to both server-side handshakes and client handshakes made by ``ConnectAsync`` or ``UpgradeToTlsAsync``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/TlsOptions.cs (ToServerOptions, ToClientOptions)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Implicit TLS
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``ServerOptions.Tls`` is set, the server shall complete a TLS handshake on every accepted connection, after any ``ConnectDelay`` and concurrency wait, before running the handler; ``IsTls`` shall then be true and a "TLS established (protocol)" event recorded.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.ImplicitTls_WithSelfSignedCertificate
- ClientTests.Tls_WithAnOnTheFlyCertificate
- TlsPinningExample.AcceptsThePinnedCertificate
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ConnectAsync speaks TLS to a TLS server
STATEMENT: >>>
``ConnectAsync`` on a server with ``ServerOptions.Tls`` shall perform the client handshake, trusting exactly the server's certificate, and return a connection with ``IsTls`` true.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.ConnectAsync_TrustsTheServersTlsCertificate
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: STARTTLS upgrade
STATEMENT: >>>
``UpgradeToTlsAsync(options)`` shall switch a plaintext connection to TLS mid-stream: a server connection shall use the given options or ``ServerOptions.Tls``; a client connection shall trust the server's certificate. Output written before the call shall be flushed in plaintext first, and after the upgrade all reads, writes, ``Input`` and ``Output`` shall go through TLS.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.StartTls_UpgradesMidConversation
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
- FtpExample.Upload_IsEncryptedEndToEnd_VerifiedThenRenamed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Upgrade preconditions
STATEMENT: >>>
``UpgradeToTlsAsync`` shall throw ``InvalidOperationException`` when no options are given and none are configured, when the connection already uses TLS, or when unread input is buffered (bytes a client pipelined after STARTTLS must not be read as plaintext).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Connection.cs (UpgradeToTlsAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test. The SMTP server checks for pipelined input itself before calling the upgrade (see ITS-CONN-020).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handshake failure handling
STATEMENT: >>>
A failed TLS handshake (certificate rejected, plaintext client, peer gone) shall record a "TLS handshake failed: reason" event and throw ``TlsHandshakeException``; on the server it shall end the connection without adding to ``Errors``. Cancellation during the handshake shall surface as ``OperationCanceledException`` instead.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A client that fails the handshake is usually exactly what a certificate-pinning or downgrade test provokes; it is the client's failure, not the stub's.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.FailedTlsHandshake_IsAnEvent_NotAHandlerError
- FtpExample.ImpostorCertificate_IsRejected
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TLS-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Transcript holds plaintext under TLS
STATEMENT: >>>
Under TLS the transcript and ``Log`` shall record the decrypted application data, not TLS records.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.ImplicitTls_WithSelfSignedCertificate
- SmtpServerTests.StartTls_RequiredBeforeMail_AndTranscriptStaysReadable
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Handlers, LineResponder and LineMatcher

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler.Echo
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Echo`` shall write every received byte back until the client closes.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ClientReset_IsRecordedButNotAnError
- ProtocolTests.ConnectAsync_TrustsTheServersTlsCertificate
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler.Hang
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Hang`` shall accept the connection and never reply (as ``Connection.HangAsync``), ending when the client disconnects or the server stops.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Hang_LetsClientTimeOut
- TcpServerTests.Dispose_StopsPromptlyEvenWithBlockedHandlers
- ConfigClientTests.a hung service times out on every attempt, then fails
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler.Reset
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Reset`` shall reset each connection as soon as it is accepted. The client may see the reset on its first read or write, or (on Linux and macOS) as a failed connect.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Reset_RefusesService
- RetryExample.RecoversFromTwoResets
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler.Close
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Close`` shall close each connection gracefully as soon as it is accepted, without sending anything.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RetryExample.GivesUpAfterThreeAttempts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler.Send
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Send(string)`` shall send the text exactly as given, with no terminator added, and ``Handler.Send(ReadOnlyMemory<byte>)`` the bytes; both shall then close the connection gracefully.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Corrupt_IsDeterministicForASeed
- RobustnessTests.WildcardBind_ClientsConnectThroughLoopback
- HttpApiExample.GarbageStatusLine_IsAnError
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The byte overload has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler.Lines and LinesAsync
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Lines`` and ``Handler.LinesAsync`` shall answer each received line with the (awaited) returned line followed by ``NewLine``, send nothing when it returns null, and end when the client closes.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Log_ReceivesLiveTraffic
- TcpServerTests.FailedAssertion_IncludesTranscript
- ConfigClientTests.garbage from the service is a protocol error and is not retried
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
``LinesAsync`` is exercised through ``Lines``, which delegates to it.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-007
STATUS: Rejected
TITLE: Rename Handler.Send to SendRaw
STATEMENT: >>>
``Handler.Send`` would be renamed ``SendRaw`` to match ``Conversation.SendRaw``.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
API churn for no behavioural gain: the documentation already states that ``Handler.Send`` sends the text exactly as given with no terminator, and there is no ``Handler`` line-sending counterpart to confuse it with.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ITS-HND-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: LineResponder greeting
STATEMENT: >>>
Lines given to ``LineResponder.Greeting`` shall be sent, in one write, as soon as a client connects and before any input is read.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: LineResponder first matching rule wins
STATEMENT: >>>
For each received line, ``LineResponder`` shall apply the first rule, in registration order, whose matcher matches the line, and answer the line in any order relative to earlier lines' rules.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
- ConfigClientTests.rule table: GET of a known and an unknown key
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: LineResponder reply forms
STATEMENT: >>>
``LineResponder.On`` shall accept a fixed reply, a reply computed from the line, an asynchronously computed reply, or (with a ``Regex``) a reply computed from the ``Match``; a null reply shall send nothing.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
- InstrumentExample.IdentifiesAndMeasures
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: LineResponder OnAndClose
STATEMENT: >>>
A rule added with ``OnAndClose`` shall send its reply, if any, then close the connection gracefully and end the handler.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: LineResponder fallback
STATEMENT: >>>
A line no rule matches shall be answered by the ``Otherwise`` reply (fixed or computed) when one is set, and ignored otherwise.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
- ConfigClientTests.rule table: GET of a known and an unknown key
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The no-fallback case has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Strings are whole-line glob patterns
STATEMENT: >>>
A string converted to ``LineMatcher`` (implicitly or with ``LineMatcher.Glob``) shall match the whole line, with ``*`` matching any run of characters and ``?`` exactly one; a string without wildcards shall therefore match only that exact line. Matching shall be case-sensitive unless ``Glob(pattern, ignoreCase: true)`` is used.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
- InstrumentExample.IdentifiesAndMeasures
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Regex matchers
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``Regex`` converted to ``LineMatcher`` (implicitly or with ``LineMatcher.FromRegex``) shall search the line, matching anywhere unless the pattern is anchored.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.LineResponder_AnswersByRule
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Exact matcher
STATEMENT: >>>
``LineMatcher.Exact(text, comparison)`` shall match only a line equal to ``text`` under ``comparison`` (ordinal by default), treating ``*`` and ``?`` as ordinary characters.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/LineMatcher.cs (Exact)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Predicate and Any matchers
STATEMENT: >>>
``LineMatcher.Where(predicate, description)`` shall match lines for which the predicate returns true, and ``LineMatcher.Any`` shall match every line.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/LineMatcher.cs (Where, Any)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-HND-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Matcher descriptions
STATEMENT: >>>
Every ``LineMatcher`` shall have a readable ``Description`` (the quoted glob, ``exactly "text"``, ``/regex/``, or the predicate's description), used in assertion, wait and conversation failure messages.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_MismatchIsReportedWithStep
- TcpServerTests.WaitFor_TimesOutWithTranscript
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Conversation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Steps run in order
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``Conversation`` shall run its steps strictly in the order they were added, once per connection, and the server shall close the connection when the script ends.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
- ConfigClientTests.scripted conversation: SET then GET, exactly in that order
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reusable across connections
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``Conversation`` instance shall hold no per-connection state, so one instance can serve several connections, each starting at step 1.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Conversation.cs (HandleAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Send lines
STATEMENT: >>>
``Send(line)`` shall send one line followed by ``NewLine``; ``Send(params lines)`` shall send several lines in one write.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SendRaw
STATEMENT: >>>
``SendRaw`` shall send text or bytes exactly as given, without a line terminator.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ClientTests.Pipeline_WritesEveryCommandBeforeAnyReply
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Expect with fixed reply
STATEMENT: >>>
``Expect(matcher)`` shall read the next line and require it to match; ``Expect(matcher, reply)`` shall additionally send ``reply`` as a line when it does.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
- ConfigClientTests.scripted conversation: SET then GET, exactly in that order
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Expect with computed reply
STATEMENT: >>>
``Expect(matcher, Func<string, string>)`` shall send, as a line, the reply computed from the matched line.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Mismatch fails the handler with the step
STATEMENT: >>>
A line that does not match an ``Expect`` step, or the client closing instead of sending it, shall fail the handler with a ``ConversationException`` whose message names the step number and description and quotes the received line (escaped), or says the client closed the connection. The failure shall appear in ``Errors``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_MismatchIsReportedWithStep
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The client-closed case has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: OnMismatch reply
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``OnMismatch(reply)`` is set, a mismatching line for any ``Expect`` overload shall first be answered with that reply, then fail as in ITS-CONV-007. No reply shall be sent when the client closed the connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_MismatchIsReportedWithStep
- RobustnessTests.Conversation_OnMismatchAppliesToComputedReplies
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ITS-CONV-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ExpectBytes
STATEMENT: >>>
``ExpectBytes(expected)`` shall read exactly ``expected.Length`` bytes and fail with a ``ConversationException`` showing both values in hex if they differ.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ClientTests.Pipeline_WritesEveryCommandBeforeAnyReply
- MutationTargetedTests.Subscribe_CountsItsDedicatedConnection
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ExpectUntil
STATEMENT: >>>
``ExpectUntil(delimiter, verify)`` shall read up to the delimiter, pass the content (without the delimiter) to ``verify`` if given, and fail with a ``ConversationException`` if the stream ends first.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: StartTls step
STATEMENT: >>>
``StartTls(options)`` shall upgrade the connection to TLS at that point in the script, using the given options or ``ServerOptions.Tls``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.StartTls_UpgradesMidConversation
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Close, Reset and Hang steps
STATEMENT: >>>
``Close()`` shall close the connection gracefully, ``Reset()`` shall abort it, and ``Hang()`` shall stop replying until the client gives up, each at that point in the script.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
- SmtpExample.GreylistingServer_SurfacesTransientFailure
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The ``Reset()`` step has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-CONV-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Delay, WithFaults and Do steps
STATEMENT: >>>
``Delay(t)`` shall pause for ``t`` (ending early when the server stops), ``WithFaults(faults)`` shall set the connection's faults from that step on, and ``Do(action, description)`` shall run arbitrary code against the connection.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Conversation.cs (Delay, WithFaults, Do)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Fault injection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Server-wide faults
STATEMENT: >>>
``ServerOptions.Faults`` shall apply to every connection the server accepts. Client connections opened with ``ConnectAsync`` shall never have faults.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Latency_DelaysWrites
- FaultTests.Fragment_SplitsWritesIntoSeparateSegments
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Per-connection faults
STATEMENT: >>>
``Connection.Faults`` shall start as ``ServerOptions.Faults`` and may be replaced at any time; the new value shall apply from the next read or write.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.FaultsCanChangePerConnection
- FtpExample.DataConnectionDroppedMidDownload_IsAnError_NotATruncatedFile
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Write latency
STATEMENT: >>>
``FaultOptions.Latency(t)`` (``WriteDelay``) shall delay every write by ``t`` before any of it is sent.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Latency_DelaysWrites
- InstrumentExample.FaultMatrix_EitherWorksOrFailsCleanly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Read delay
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReadDelay`` shall delay each read from the underlying transport.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/Internal/TapStream.cs (ReadAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connect delay
STATEMENT: >>>
``ConnectDelay`` shall hold an accepted connection silent for that long before the TLS handshake (if any) and the handler run.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.ConnectDelay_HoldsTheGreeting
- InstrumentExample.FaultMatrix_EitherWorksOrFailsCleanly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fragmentation
STATEMENT: >>>
``FaultOptions.Fragment(size, delay)`` shall split every write into separately sent and separately recorded chunks of at most ``size`` bytes, pausing ``delay`` between chunks.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Fragment_SplitsWritesIntoSeparateSegments
- BinaryProtocolExample.ReassemblesAFrameDeliveredOneByteAtATime
- Hl7MllpExample.AckDribbledOutOneByteAtATime_IsReassembled
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Disconnect after N bytes with reset
STATEMENT: >>>
``FaultOptions.DisconnectAfter(n)`` shall send exactly the first ``n`` bytes written on the connection (cutting mid-write if needed), record a "fault: disconnect after n bytes written" event, reset the connection, and end the handler with a ``ConnectionTerminatedException`` that is not counted as an error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_ResetsMidMessage
- InstrumentExample.FaultMatrix_EitherWorksOrFailsCleanly
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Disconnect after N bytes with close
STATEMENT: >>>
With ``DisconnectMode.Close`` the fault shall close the connection with FIN instead, so the client reads exactly ``n`` bytes then end of stream.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_CloseMode_SendsEndOfStream
- BinaryProtocolExample.TruncatedFrame_IsEndOfStream
- ConfigClientTests.a reply cut mid-line is an error, not a truncated value
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Disconnect fault through Output
STATEMENT: >>>
The disconnect fault shall apply equally to data flushed through ``Connection.Output``, and the close shall be recorded exactly once.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.DisconnectAfterViaOutput_StillRecordsTheClose
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: TransformWrite
STATEMENT: >>>
``TransformWrite`` shall replace each outgoing buffer with the function's result before corruption, fragmentation and the disconnect limit are applied.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- BinaryProtocolExample.InsaneLengthPrefix_IsRejectedBeforeAllocating
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Corruption
STATEMENT: >>>
``FaultOptions.Corrupt(rate, seed)`` shall flip one random bit in roughly ``rate`` of written bytes, preserving the length. A rate outside 0 to 1 shall throw ``ArgumentOutOfRangeException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Corrupt_IsDeterministicForASeed
- HedgehogProperties.Client_SurvivesCorruptReplies
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Deterministic corruption per connection
STATEMENT: >>>
Each connection shall draw corruption from its own generator seeded from ``CorruptSeed`` and the connection ``Id``, so the same options produce the same corrupted bytes on every run and every server, however connections interleave and however often a ``FaultOptions`` instance is reused.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.Corrupt_SameOptionsGiveTheSameBytesOnEveryServer
- FaultTests.Corrupt_IsDeterministicForASeed
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-FAULT-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Faults apply to plaintext under TLS
STATEMENT: >>>
On a TLS connection faults shall act on the application plaintext: byte counts are application bytes, and the TLS handshake shall not be affected.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FtpExample.DataConnectionDroppedMidDownload_IsAnError_NotATruncatedFile
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Covered only indirectly (a disconnect fault on a TLS-protected FTP data connection); no test checks byte counts under TLS.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Transcripts and assertions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Server transcript lists every connection
STATEMENT: >>>
``ServerTranscript.Connections`` (and the zero-based indexer) shall list a ``ConnectionTranscript`` for every accepted connection, in accept order. ``AssertConnectionCount(n)`` shall fail unless exactly ``n`` connections were accepted.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Sequential_HandlesOneConnectionAtATime
- RetryExample.GivesUpAfterThreeAttempts
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Traffic recorded in order
STATEMENT: >>>
A ``ConnectionTranscript`` shall record, in order and with timestamps, every chunk of bytes received and sent and every event, available as ``Entries``; ``ReceivedBytes``, ``SentBytes``, ``ReceivedText`` and ``SentText`` shall concatenate the traffic in each direction.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.Fragment_SplitsWritesIntoSeparateSegments
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_ResetsMidMessage
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connection events
STATEMENT: >>>
``Events`` shall list the connection's events, including "connected from", "closed", "closed by peer", "reset", "reset by peer", "TLS established", "TLS handshake failed", "read timed out", "hanging", "fault: disconnect" and "handler failed".
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- FaultTests.DisconnectAfter_ResetsMidMessage
- RobustnessTests.PeerResetDuringAWrite_IsRecordedAsAReset
- ProtocolTests.ImplicitTls_WithSelfSignedCertificate
- RobustnessTests.FailedTlsHandshake_IsAnEvent_NotAHandlerError
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: IsClosed
STATEMENT: >>>
``ConnectionTranscript.IsClosed`` shall become true once either side closes or resets the connection, and stay false while it is open.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- RobustnessTests.Hang_IgnoresReadTimeout
- TcpServerTests.ClientReset_IsRecordedButNotAnError
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Byte recording can be turned off
STATEMENT: >>>
With ``ServerOptions.RecordTranscript`` false, sent and received bytes shall not be stored; events and messages shall still be recorded and ``Log`` shall still be called.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreRecorded_EvenWithByteRecordingOff
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Lines
STATEMENT: >>>
``ReceivedLines`` and ``SentLines`` shall list complete LF- or CRLF-terminated lines with the terminator removed; once the connection is closed a trailing unterminated line shall be included too. On ``ServerTranscript`` they shall concatenate all connections' lines in connection order.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- TcpServerTests.Concurrent_HandlesClientsInParallel
- ConfigClientTests.rule table: GET of a known and an unknown key
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Decoded messages
STATEMENT: >>>
``RecordMessage(direction, message)`` shall record a decoded protocol message, kept apart from raw bytes and lines and listed by ``ReceivedMessages`` and ``SentMessages``; ``TranscriptDirection.Event`` shall record an event instead.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
- Hl7MllpExample.Messages_AreAcknowledged_OnOneConnection
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Line assertions
STATEMENT: >>>
``HasReceivedLine`` and ``HasSentLine`` shall report whether any line matches; ``AssertReceivedLine``, ``AssertNotReceivedLine`` and ``AssertSentLine`` shall throw ``TranscriptAssertionException`` when the expectation fails.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- TcpServerTests.FailedAssertion_IncludesTranscript
- FtpExample.ServerWithoutTls_IsRefused_NotDowngraded
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: In-order assertions
STATEMENT: >>>
``AssertReceivedLinesInOrder``, ``AssertSentLinesInOrder`` and ``AssertReceivedMessagesInOrder`` shall pass when the matchers match lines (or messages) in that order, other entries allowed between them, and otherwise fail naming the first matcher not found.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- ProtocolTests.Conversation_ScriptsAnSmtpSession
- InstrumentExample.IdentifiesAndMeasures
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
``AssertSentLinesInOrder`` has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Message assertions
STATEMENT: >>>
``HasReceivedMessage``, ``HasSentMessage``, ``AssertReceivedMessage``, ``AssertNotReceivedMessage`` and ``AssertSentMessage`` shall behave as the line assertions, over decoded messages.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
- MessageTranscriptTests.FailedMessageAssertion_ShowsTheMessagesInTheDump
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Text assertion
STATEMENT: >>>
``AssertReceived(text)`` shall pass when the received text contains ``text`` (ordinal), regardless of line structure.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SmtpExample.SendsWelcomeMail
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Failures include the transcript
STATEMENT: >>>
A failed transcript assertion shall throw ``TranscriptAssertionException`` whose message states the expectation and contains the full transcript dump, or "Transcript is empty.".
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.FailedAssertion_IncludesTranscript
- MessageTranscriptTests.FailedMessageAssertion_ShowsTheMessagesInTheDump
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Wait helpers
STATEMENT: >>>
``WaitForReceivedLineAsync``, ``WaitForSentLineAsync``, ``WaitForReceivedMessageAsync``, ``WaitForSentMessageAsync`` and ``WaitUntilAsync(condition, description)`` shall complete as soon as the condition holds, re-checking whenever anything is recorded rather than polling, with a default timeout of 5 seconds.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Stream_CanBeUsedWithStandardReaders
- TcpServerTests.Concurrent_HandlesClientsInParallel
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Wait timeout and cancellation
STATEMENT: >>>
A wait that times out shall throw ``TimeoutException`` naming what was awaited and including the transcript dump; cancelling the caller's token shall end the wait with ``OperationCanceledException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.WaitFor_TimesOutWithTranscript
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The cancellation case has no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Connection-count waits
STATEMENT: >>>
``WaitForConnectionsAsync(n)`` shall wait until at least ``n`` connections have been accepted; ``WaitForClosedConnectionsAsync(n)`` until at least ``n`` have been accepted and all accepted connections are closed; ``ConnectionTranscript.WaitForCloseAsync`` until that connection is closed.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Dispose_StopsPromptlyEvenWithBlockedHandlers
- TcpServerTests.ReadmeExample_RepliesOnEphemeralPort
- SmtpServerTests.Intercept_421_ClosesTheConnection
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Readable dump
STATEMENT: >>>
``ToString`` of a transcript shall print one line per protocol line, prefixed ``#id <-`` (received) or ``#id ->`` (sent), merging chunks split across reads and escaping control characters; events as ``#id --``; messages as ``#id <=`` or ``#id =>``; and mark a trailing partial line "(no newline)".
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Transcript_ToString_IsReadable
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreKeptApartFromBytes_AndAssertable
- MemcachedExample.SetThenGet_GoldenTranscript
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Live log
STATEMENT: >>>
When ``ServerOptions.Log`` is set it shall receive each recorded chunk (``#id <- escaped text``), event and message as it is recorded, and before it becomes visible in the transcript.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- TcpServerTests.Log_ReceivesLiveTraffic
- MessageTranscriptTests.Messages_AreRecorded_EvenWithByteRecordingOff
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-TR-018
STATUS: Deferred
TITLE: Cap on transcript growth
STATEMENT: >>>
A server should be able to bound the memory its transcript uses, for example by keeping only the most recent traffic, so a long-running stub does not grow without limit.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Transcripts currently keep every byte for the server's lifetime, which is right for short tests. Bounding them changes what assertions and dumps can rely on, so it is a design change left for later; ``RecordTranscript = false`` is the current workaround.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ITS-TR-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: UDP server

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Listening
STATEMENT: >>>
``UdpServer.Listen(port, handler, options)`` shall bind ``127.0.0.1`` (port 0 picking a free port) and ``Listen(IPEndPoint, ...)`` the given endpoint, and start receiving before returning; ``EndPoint`` and ``Port`` shall report the bound address.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpServerTests.Replies_ToEachDatagram
- DnsExample.ResolvesARecords_OverUdp
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Host
STATEMENT: >>>
``UdpServer.Host`` shall map a wildcard bind to the matching loopback address, as ``TcpServer.Host`` does.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/UdpServer.cs (Host)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Datagrams and replies
STATEMENT: >>>
The handler shall receive each datagram as a ``Datagram`` with ``Data``, ``Text`` (decoded with ``UdpServerOptions.Encoding``), ``RemoteEndPoint`` and a ``CancellationToken`` cancelled on stop; ``ReplyAsync`` shall send bytes or text back to the sender, and ``UdpServer.SendAsync`` may send to any endpoint. Sent datagrams shall be recorded.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpServerTests.Replies_ToEachDatagram
- DnsExample.SpoofedReplyWithTheWrongId_IsIgnored
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reply delay
STATEMENT: >>>
``UdpServerOptions.ReplyDelay`` shall delay every reply and ``SendAsync`` by that amount.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/UdpServer.cs (SendAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Handler concurrency
STATEMENT: >>>
Handlers shall run one at a time in arrival order by default; ``MaxConcurrency = n`` shall allow up to ``n`` at once. A ``MaxConcurrency`` below 1 shall throw ``ArgumentOutOfRangeException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpServerTests.Replies_ToEachDatagram
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Only the default (sequential) mode is exercised; parallel handling and validation have no automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reproducible packet loss
STATEMENT: >>>
``DropRate`` shall silently drop that fraction of incoming datagrams, chosen by a generator seeded with ``Seed`` so the same traffic loses the same datagrams on every run. Dropped datagrams shall be recorded with ``Dropped`` true and excluded from ``Received``. A ``DropRate`` outside 0 to 1 shall throw ``ArgumentOutOfRangeException``.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpServerTests.DropRate_LosesDatagramsReproducibly
- UdpTelemetryExample.Metrics_TolerateHeavyPacketLoss
- DnsExample.PacketLoss_IsRiddenOutWithRetries
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: UDP transcript
STATEMENT: >>>
``UdpTranscript`` shall expose ``Records``, ``Received``, ``Sent``, ``ReceivedTexts`` and ``SentTexts``; ``AssertReceived(matcher)`` shall fail with ``TranscriptAssertionException`` including the transcript; ``WaitForReceivedAsync``, ``WaitForSentAsync`` and ``WaitUntilAsync`` shall wait as the stream transcript waits do.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpServerTests.Replies_ToEachDatagram
- UdpTelemetryExample.Metrics_AreWellFormed
- UdpTelemetryExample.Syslog_UsesRfc5424Format
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: UDP handler errors
STATEMENT: >>>
An exception from a UDP handler shall be added to ``UdpServer.Errors``, logged, and not stop the server; ``ThrowIfFaulted`` shall throw an ``AggregateException`` of them.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- UdpServerTests.HandlerErrors_AreCaptured
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oversized datagrams
STATEMENT: >>>
The receive buffer shall be ``MaxDatagramSize`` bytes (default 65,527). Where the OS reports a larger datagram as an error (Windows) it shall be discarded and logged as "datagram larger than MaxDatagramSize"; where the OS truncates it silently (Unix) the truncated datagram shall be delivered.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/UdpServer.cs (ReceiveLoopAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Receive loop survives ICMP errors
STATEMENT: >>>
An ICMP "port unreachable" caused by replying to a vanished client shall not stop the receive loop (on Windows ``SIO_UDP_CONNRESET`` shall be disabled; other receive errors shall be skipped).
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/UdpServer.cs (Listen, ReceiveLoopAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-UDP-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: UDP stop
STATEMENT: >>>
``StopAsync`` and ``DisposeAsync`` shall cancel every ``Datagram.CancellationToken``, close the socket, skip datagrams queued but not yet dispatched, ignore handler exceptions raised during the stop, and wait at most ``ShutdownTimeout`` for running handlers. Repeated calls shall return the same stop operation.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- Review: src/Intertube.Stub/UdpServer.cs (StopCoreAsync, DispatchLoopAsync)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No automated test.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
